VERDICT: REJECTED

The change does not complete the stated theme-wide refactor and introduces two simultaneous announcement bars. `MainLayout` now renders the new settings-backed `AnnouncementBar` while retaining `ShippingBanner`, whose three hardcoded rotating marketing messages remain visible. Enabling an admin announcement therefore displays both bars rather than making the existing announcement area admin-editable.

The dynamic Tailwind namespace and CSS variables are valid and the frontend production build succeeds, but the claimed user-site coverage is materially incomplete: the source still contains hundreds of hardcoded public color utilities (291 matches outside admin), including public order/status UI and numerous remaining pages/components. TVERDICT: REJECTED
his conflicts directly with the attached requirement that every user-facing visual style react to Theme Builder changes. Several unchanged global defaults and toast colors are also fixed, so a theme switch cannot update the entire storefront as claimed.

